# Master Data

## Purpose

Master Data provides the governed reference information used throughout the Supply Chain Decision Intelligence Platform.

This data supports inventory planning, supplier management, forecasting, analytics, AI agents, and executive reporting.

Master Data represents business entities that change infrequently and are reused across multiple business processes.

---

# Branch Master

## Description

Contains branch and regional information used throughout the platform.

## Attributes

- Branch ID
- Branch Name
- Region
- State

## Example

| Branch ID | Branch Name | Region | State |
|------------|------------|--------|--------|
| B001 | Abingdon | East | VA |
| B002 | Chesapeake | East | VA |
| B003 | Richmond | East | VA |

---

# Product Family Master

## Description

Defines the highest level of the product hierarchy used for strategic supply chain planning and executive reporting.

## Attributes

- Product Family ID
- Product Family Name

## Example

| Product Family ID | Product Family |
|-------------------|---------------|
| PF001 | Excavation |
| PF002 | Earthmoving |
| PF003 | Material Handling |
| PF004 | Power Systems |
| PF005 | Road Construction |

---

# Product Category Master

## Description

Defines product categories within a product family.

## Attributes

- Product Category ID
- Product Category Name
- Product Family ID

## Example

| Product Category ID | Product Category | Product Family |
|--------------------|------------------|---------------|
| PC001 | Excavators | Excavation |
| PC002 | Dozers | Earthmoving |
| PC003 | Wheel Loaders | Earthmoving |

---

# Product Master

## Description

Contains all products managed within the supply chain network.

## Attributes

- Product ID
- Product Name
- Product Category
- Product Family
- Criticality

## Example

| Product ID | Product Name | Product Category | Product Family | Criticality |
|------------|--------------|------------------|---------------|-------------|
| P001 | CAT 320 | Excavators | Excavation | High |
| P002 | CAT 336 | Excavators | Excavation | High |
| P003 | CAT D6 | Dozers | Earthmoving | Medium |

---

# Supplier Master

## Description

Contains supplier reference information used for procurement and supplier performance analytics.

## Attributes

- Supplier ID
- Supplier Name
- Supplier Tier
- Lead Time

## Example

| Supplier ID | Supplier Name | Tier | Lead Time (Days) |
|------------|--------------|------|------------------|
| S001 | Caterpillar Manufacturing | Tier 1 | 15 |
| S002 | Midwest Components | Tier 2 | 10 |

---

# Equipment Master

## Description

Contains equipment model information associated with supported products.

## Attributes

- Equipment ID
- Equipment Model
- Equipment Family

## Example

| Equipment ID | Equipment Model | Equipment Family |
|-------------|----------------|------------------|
| E001 | CAT 320 | Excavators |
| E002 | CAT D6 | Dozers |

---

# Master Data Hierarchy

Business reporting and analytics follow the hierarchy below:

Product Family
↓
Product Category
↓
Product
↓
Equipment

Example:

Excavation
↓
Excavators
↓
CAT 320
↓
Individual Equipment Units

Earthmoving
↓
Dozers
↓
CAT D6
↓
Individual Equipment Units

---

# Business Purpose

Master Data serves as the foundation for:

- Data Quality Validation
- Curated Analytics Models
- Forecasting
- Inventory Optimization
- Supplier Performance Analysis
- AI Agent Recommendations
- Executive Decision Support

Master Data integrates with ERP systems, operational databases, business-managed files, and external data sources to create a unified supply chain decision intelligence platform.
